--- explained
Target reds: test 28 (an approved event exists although the death came inside set_aside) and test 29 (approval events exist although step 10 failed). Also red, one cause: ledger_states now runs after the new approval, so the captured states hold the new digest. Test 2 asserts the old digest in the group's states, test 3 asserts the folder's state is yours, and tests 9 (both) and 11 assert that the compensating events restore the old digest or status.
Collateral, in every log: 11 FAIL lines from tests/test_action.py CanaryActionTests. Any edit under canary/ changes a file scanner/manifest.json hashes, so scripts/action.py scanner_manifest() exits 2 with "the bundled scanner failed its integrity check" (quoted in the tracebacks below). Five of the class's six methods go red (11 FAIL lines with subtests); the sixth, test_an_unlisted_module_in_a_subfolder_is_refused, expects exit 2 and stays green.

